  "body": "From the review of PR #90 (#84). drill_reach drops stock above the R plane, deferring to the rapid laws, but verify's rapid law (d) only covers sideways rapids (crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs:14). If an R plane is set below an unfaced stock top, the vertical rapid down to R passes through stock, and no law may catch it - a collision. The depth check also under-counts by the gap between stock top and R.\n\nFirst prove it: a drill op whose R plane sits below the declared stock top. If the post is not blocked, raise this to P0. Done means: a rapid down through stock to the R plane blocks the post by name (or drilling refuses an R plane inside stock at generation).",
